;; Package abi is the guest's hypercall ABI as Go constants (doc/GUEST.md,
;; *The hypercall ABI*): the doorbell's address, the call numbers and the
;; call block's layout -- what guest/rt/rt.c spells in C for the C guest,
;; and what the Go guest (guest/tamago, built with TamaGo) imports.  It
;; imports nothing, so that a GOOS=tamago build can use it; vmm's test holds
;; the monitor's own numbers to it.
(in-ns 'go.arbace.box.abi) (go/file "abi.go" :doc "Package abi is the guest's hypercall ABI as Go constants (doc/GUEST.md,\n*The hypercall ABI*): the doorbell's address, the call numbers and the\ncall block's layout -- what guest/rt/rt.c spells in C for the C guest,\nand what the Go guest (guest/tamago, built with TamaGo) imports.  It\nimports nothing, so that a GOOS=tamago build can use it; vmm's test holds\nthe monitor's own numbers to it.\n" :imports [])




