(go/const "The network (Arbace's doc/go/BOX-NOTES.md, S5), from 40: TCP streams\nthe monitor makes on the guest's behalf, under the policy its launcher\ngives it, named by handles (0 up).  No call waits: a dial and a lookup\nrun in the monitor while the guest goes on, a connection's bytes are\nread into the monitor's buffer as they come and written from it, and a\ncall that has nothing yet answers EAGAIN; the guest polls NetEvents\nwhile it waits.  Not host functions: not serialised with the others.\nAn answer below 0 is -errno (Linux's numbers: EAGAIN nothing yet,\nEBADF no such handle, EINPROGRESS not done yet, EPERM a dial the policy\nrefuses, EACCES a listen it refuses) or one of NetErr*.  Without a\nnetwork every call answers -1.  Addresses are host:port strings, the\nhost an IP literal ([v6]), empty for every address.\n"


  ^{:line 117} [^{:val 40 :doc "NetInfo: ret 0 when the box has a network, and a[0] the host's\nfamilies: 1 IPv4, 2 IPv6, their sum.\n"} NetInfo (+ iota 40)]



